    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0566" n="532" xml:id="pg532"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 282.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to further reply to the
                    oral communication of Mr. Soler of the 2d instant and to his note of the same
                    date notifying this Department that the steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dauntless</hi> proposed to set out the next day on a filibustering
                    expedition. In this connection Mr. Soler said: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Remembering the orders which the Government of the United States has
                            given, that an officer of its Navy be present in person upon the said
                            vessel and watch her, I have also to inform your excellency that this
                            legation has learned that the aforesaid officer has not considered
                            himself obliged to go on board because the arms which were on the <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Dauntless</hi> have been landed and she is now
                            in ballast.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Mr. Soler’s communication having been referred to the Secretary of the Navy, I am
                    to-day informed by the Acting Secretary that no orders have ever been issued by
                    his Department directing a United States naval officer to be present on board
                    that vessel, and that there is not at the present time an officer available for
                    such service at Jacksonville.</p>
                <p>It would appear from this that there is some confusion in the mind of Mr. Soler
                    between a naval-marine and a revenue-marine officer, the latter acting, as you
                    are aware, under direction of the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
